---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility" description="How lirazhazala.com is built to be usable by everyone, and how to report a barrier.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-[clamp(16px,5vw,56px)] pt-[clamp(40px,8vw,84px)] pb-8">
    <header class="grid gap-2 max-w-[60ch] pb-6">
      <h1 class="m-0 text-[clamp(34px,5vw,56px)] leading-[1.08] tracking-[-0.03em] font-semibold">Accessibility</h1>
      <p class="m-0 text-[18px] leading-[1.6] text-muted">
        Accessibility on this site is part of the design, not a checklist at the end. This page says what I aimed for, how I built it, and how to tell me when I missed.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="statement grid gap-6 max-w-[68ch]">
      <section aria-labelledby="target">
        <h2 id="target">The target</h2>
        <p>This site aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="built-in">
        <h2 id="built-in">What is built in</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A "Skip to content" link, clear page landmarks, and one main heading per page.</li>
          <li>A visible focus ring on every link and button, so you always know where you are when using a keyboard.</li>
          <li>Touch targets of at least 44 by 44 pixels.</li>
          <li>Text colors that meet or exceed a 4.5 to 1 contrast ratio in both light and dark themes.</li>
          <li>Light and dark themes that follow your device setting, with a switch in the navigation that remembers your choice.</li>
          <li>When your device asks for reduced motion, nothing on the site moves. You see the final state straight away.</li>
          <li>Color never carries meaning on its own. The current page, the current section and every status also use shape, weight or text.</li>
          <li>Pages work without JavaScript. Scripts only add enhancements.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="known">
        <h2 id="known">Known gaps</h2>
        <p>I audited every page in October 2026. This is what I know is not right yet.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The clay objects on the home page can be picked up only with a mouse or a finger, and their names appear only on hover. Screen readers get the same names as a list, but sighted keyboard users don't see them yet.</li>
          <li>The case-study recordings are silent product clips, and the text beside each one describes what it shows. The ones on the AeroPulse and Waypoint pages have a pause button, but the phone recordings and short clips on the Neta and Recall pages, and the recordings on the home page cards, don't yet. They play only while they are on screen, and stay still if your device asks for reduced motion.</li>
          <li>My CV PDF is tagged and has real text, but a screen reader reads its two columns mixed together and its headings as plain text. The About page covers the same path in order, and if you need the CV in another format, ask me and I'll send one.</li>
          <li>The live demos of AeroPulse and Waypoint are separate apps that the case studies link out to. They are working prototypes, and I haven't audited them to the same standard as this site.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="report">
        <h2 id="report">Tell me about a barrier</h2>
        <p>
          If something on this site gets in your way, I want to know. Reach me through the <a class="prose-link" href="#contact">contact details below</a>, say which page and what happened, and I will reply and fix it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-[14px] text-muted">Last reviewed: October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .statement section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .statement h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 28px);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .statement p,
  .statement ul {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .statement ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.25em;
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .statement li::marker {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
